  "reason": "The records collectively make the later approach plausibly reconstructible. Multiple studies already combine elemental-powder mechanical alloying or high-energy ball milling under argon with short-duration vacuum SPS, including milling times near 5–6 h and Ti-containing equimolar HEAs. They also show that milling time controls phase homogenization, crystallite refinement, and contamination, while SPS produces dense bulk material. Separate records explicitly attribute high hardness and compressive strength to nanocrystalline grain-boundary and solid-solution strengthening, and work on the closely related Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni-Ti family identifies Ti atomic size as a driver of phase formation and strength. Although no record presents the exact CoCrFeNiTi composition, low SPS temperature, 83/17 FCC-BCC ratio, and full property combination, an expert could reasonably combine the established processing route with the Ti/phase and nanograin-strengthening teachings to propose the later intervention and mechanism."
